    "body": "### Problem\n\nCertain file modification via e.g. `:tabnew | term sh` doesn't seem to trigger `'autoread'`, requiring additional `:checktime`.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n* `echo foo > testfile`\n* `nvim --clean testfile`\n* Edit the content, don't save.\n* `:!mv testfile testfile2`, E211 will show up (expected).\n* `:tabnew | term sh`, in terminal mode run `touch testfile2 && mv testfile2 testfile`\n* `exit` or ctrl+d, then press any key to close terminal buffer.\n\nModified buffer state will be shown, attempting to save will show \"WARNING: The file has been changed since reading it!!!\"\n\nNote: this is a contrived example, in reality I keep running into this issue after switching branches with `:tabnew | term lazygit`.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nAfter closing terminal buffer, `'autoread'` triggers W12 and prompt to reload the file (which is what would happen if I do `:term sh` instead of `:tabnew | term sh`).\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nCurrent latest commit in master, ce5e230a\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nN/A\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nLinux\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nfoot 1.28.0\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nfoot\n\n### Installation\n\nBuild from source",
